(7541733, 1206652, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>A great image that contributes to the challenge well<br/> <br/>Cor blimey Janine, I think you caught that just in time! What a cracker for the challenge theme. As for Skips comments, Im not sure what he means about the shadow spread on the antenna? And as far as the halos are concerned is that the result of the sharpening? Anyway, congratulations on the ribbon, well deserved. Title? What about Bleak House or just a little TLC needed<br/></td>', 'Hello from the critique club A great image that contributes to the challenge well Cor blimey Janine, I think you caught that just in time! What a cracker for the challenge theme. As for Skips comments, Im not sure what he means about the shadow spread on the antenna? And as far as the halos are concerned is that the result of the sharpening? Anyway, congratulations on the ribbon, well deserved. Title? What about Bleak House or just a little TLC needed', '2017-10-31 09:29:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(7541734, 1206817, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>Your subject is certainly appropriate for the challenge it looks well abandoned. The ground growth in front of the building certainly confirms its abandoned status whilst the tree growth looks a little detached from the building itself it also identifies it as abandoned. I think your composition would have worked better to place the doorway to the left so that we have the decrepit state of the building balanced by the lovely splash of colour on the right I just think it would look a bit more interesting?</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that meets the challenge Your subject is certainly appropriate for the challenge it looks well abandoned. The ground growth in front of the building certainly confirms its abandoned status whilst the tree growth looks a little detached from the building itself it also identifies it as abandoned. I think your composition would have worked better to place the doorway to the left so that we have the decrepit state of the building balanced by the lovely splash of colour on the right I just think it would look a bit more interesting?', '2017-10-31 09:37:20.000000', NULL, 0),
